## Ipark Hyundai Development Company financial statements, 6 years: Revenue went from KRW 3.67tn to KRW 4.15tn and became 1.13x

The consolidated financial statements in the 2020–2025 annual reports that Ipark Hyundai Development Company (294870) filed with Korea's DART electronic disclosure system, laid out by year. Figures from the 2026 half-year report cover a different period and are shown separately. **Every figure below is taken as filed in the DART submissions; there is no interpretation or outlook.** Amounts are in Korean won (KRW; bn = billion, tn = trillion).

### 1. Income statement — revenue peaked in 2024

| Fiscal year | Revenue | Revenue change | Operating income | Op. income change | Operating margin | Net income |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | 3.67tn | — | 585.7bn | — | 16.0% | 220.2bn |
| 2021 | 3.36tn | −8.35% | 273.4bn | −53.32% | 8.1% | 176.3bn |
| 2022 | 3.30tn | −1.95% | 116.4bn | −57.44% | 3.5% | 50.2bn |
| 2023 | 4.19tn | +27.06% | 195.3bn | +67.82% | 4.7% | 172.9bn |
| 2024 | 4.26tn | +1.56% | 184.6bn | −5.47% | 4.3% | 155.7bn |
| 2025 | 4.15tn | −2.57% | 248.6bn | +34.65% | 6.0% | 158.1bn |

Revenue was largest in 2024 at KRW 4.26tn and smallest in 2022 at KRW 3.30tn among the six years. It fell from the previous year 3 times: 2021 (−8.35%), 2022 (−1.95%), 2025 (−2.57%).

Operating income was largest in 2020 at KRW 585.7bn and smallest in 2022 at KRW 116.4bn. The operating margin was highest in 2020 at 16.0%.

**Net income was largest in 2020 at KRW 220.2bn and smallest in 2022 at KRW 50.2bn.**

### 2. Financial position — equity became 1.17x

| Fiscal year | Total assets | Total equity | Debt ratio | Current ratio |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | 6.12tn | 2.74tn | 123.0% | 192.4% |
| 2021 | 6.57tn | 2.89tn | 127.6% | 174.1% |
| 2022 | 7.34tn | 2.90tn | 152.8% | 157.3% |
| 2023 | 7.02tn | 3.01tn | 133.2% | 158.4% |
| 2024 | 7.46tn | 3.11tn | 139.6% | 153.3% |
| 2025 | 7.60tn | 3.21tn | 136.5% | 143.3% |

The debt ratio was highest in 2022 at 152.8% and lowest in 2020 at 123.0%.

Over the same period total assets went from KRW 6.12tn to KRW 7.60tn (1.24x), and **total equity went from KRW 2.74tn to KRW 3.21tn and became 1.17x.**

The current ratio was above 100% in all six years, ranging from 143.3% to 192.4%.

### 3. Cash flow — negative in 2 years

| Fiscal year | Operating cash flow | Net income | Operating CF ÷ net income | ROE |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | −258.9bn | 220.2bn | −1.18x | 8.0% |
| 2021 | 30.4bn | 176.3bn | 0.17x | 6.1% |
| 2022 | −1.74tn | 50.2bn | −34.55x | 1.7% |
| 2023 | 640.2bn | 172.9bn | 3.70x | 5.8% |
| 2024 | 314.4bn | 155.7bn | 2.02x | 5.0% |
| 2025 | 2.8bn | 158.1bn | 0.02x | 4.9% |

Operating cash flow was negative in 2020 and 2022. It was largest in 2023 at KRW 640.2bn.

ROE was highest in 2020 at 8.0% and lowest in 2022 at 1.7%.

### 4. Latest half-year report (end of H1, 9th fiscal period, consolidated basis)

**The period differs, so these figures cannot be compared directly with the annual tables above.** Only cumulative figures for the same period of the previous year are compared.

| Item | 2026 cumulative | Same period last year | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Revenue | 1.59tn | 2.07tn | −23.22% |
| Operating income | 202.9bn | 134.3bn | +51.07% |
| Net income | 133.0bn | 106.9bn | +24.45% |
| Finance income | 3.5bn | 3.2bn | +10.55% |
| Operating cash flow | 461.9bn | −214.6bn | **turned to profit** |

At the end of the period, total assets were KRW 7.52tn, total liabilities KRW 4.23tn and total equity KRW 3.29tn.

The cumulative operating margin was 12.8%.

No rate of change is computed for operating cash flow, because the sign changed between the two periods.

